Hobbes's reasoning sets the bar required to make the argument that anarchy works better than you think on the floor.
 Reasoning about anarchy and government that incorporates the foregoing considerations sets that bar higher, but only a few inches so.
 Even persons who recognize self-governance's existence quickly follow their recognition with the caveat that self-governance's scope of effective application is severely limited.
 And even persons who acknowledge that some governments are truly horrendous are still sure that any government is better than none at all.
